                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_435">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        Merton College</orgName><p>‘Liber domus scolarium de Merton’ in Oxon’ de
                        legato M. Ioh’ Reynham sacre pagine professoris et quondam socii eiusdem
                        domus’ (fol. 115v)‘Hugo Herle habet librum particularem’ (fol. 204v)‘Iste
                        liber emptus fuit [pro l ... florinis]’ (fol. 204v)‘Iohanni Cole’ (fol.
                        201v)At least the first part of the MS was at the College by early s. xiv
                        (UO46.54). CBMLC 16, 785 thus identifies the donor as a different John
                        Reyham (fl. 1321–1331), fellow of Merton (BRUO 1570) from the Reynham (d.
                        1376) who gave many other MSS. However, there is nothing to associate this
                        MS with the name of John Reynham at all beyond the inscription on fol. 115v,
                        the form of which does not support this interpretation. Perhaps the latter
                        part of the MS was given by John Reynham (d. 1376).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">John Reynham (d. by Nov. 1376), fellow of
                     Merton and chancellor of Oxford</provenance>
               </history>
